                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "How do I explain this game? It's definitely a fighting game, but not your typical fighter. I would consider this a good party game. It's not serious, awkwardly hilarious and most of all, fun. The controls are simple, basically no learning curve, and one of the best things missing from many of today's multiplayer games these days, playing with your friends on the same screen while sitting on a comfy couch. Not the best game out there by any means, but it is a good time. A friend of mine introduced this game to me at a LAN recently, and after a few rounds I started seeing the charm within this cheese filled fight club. It reminds me of some late 90s/early 2000s video games that I would play on my Dreamcast, PS2 or Xbox. They didn't take themselves as seriously as they do today. The art reminds me of Jet Set Radio or Crazy Taxi. I know that sounds weird, but I don't think I am alone on that.",
